#include <Types.r>resource 'STR#' (129, "User Text combat strings") {	{	/* array StringArray: 180 elements */	/* Humanoid */		/* [1] */		"You ready your %uweapon and prepare yourself for "		"your opponent's next move.",		/* [2] */		"Your wounds ache as you fear the human reject just "		"might be able to take it.",		/* [3] */		"You circle your prey, unable to suppress a giggle.  "		"It's no match for you.",		/* [4] */		"Only slightly shaken, you feel anything can happen "		"at this point.  There is no advantage for the "		"%mname or yourself.",		/* [5] */		"You smile and kiss your %uweapon.  Grinning, you "		"decide to finish the %mname.",		/* [6] */		"You stagger and ready your %uweapon, praying that "		"you'll make it home alive.",		/* [7] */		"Slightly battered, you clutch your %uweapon and "		"prepare to turn your luck around.",		/* [8] */		"You're feeling a bit out of it as well, but you're "		"in far better condition than that sniveling %mname.",		/* [9] */		"Badly in need of rest yourself, you hold your hand "		"to your side in pain.",/* Orc */		/* [10] */		"You ready your %uweapon and prepare yourself for "		"the orc's next move.",		/* [11] */		"You nearly collapse as you realize you are almost "		"dead...",		/* [12] */		"The %mname was no match for a superior human such "		"as yourself.",		/* [13] */		"You eye the %mname's weapon warily.",		/* [14] */		"You feel adrenaline course through your veins, and "		"prepare for the death of the vile %mname.",		/* [15] */		"You feel the crushing eyes of Athos looking down "		"upon you unhappily.",		/* [16] */		"a trifle hurt, you resolve that Betse, your "		"%uweapon will finish this orcish fiend.",		/* [17] */		"Slashed a few times, you think to yourself that "		"THIS orc deserves everything\nyou choose to give "		"it, and more...",		/* [18] */		"Feeling death near, your breathing becomes "		"irregular.",/* Goblin */		/* [19] */		"You almost laugh at the goblin, thinking of an ape "		"with green skin.",		/* [20] */		"You feel faint from blood loss, and realize that "		"soon you may be dead.",		/* [21] */		"Battle never felt so good.  You will easily defeat "		"the puny goblin.",		/* [22] */		"At this point, anything can happen.",		/* [23] */		"Grim, you close, finishing what you've started...",		/* [24] */		"Blood dripping down your side, you defend yourself "		"as best you can.",		/* [25] */		"Slightly in pain, you think that this monster "		"doesn't yet know who it is dealing with...",		/* [26] */		"You'll have this fight resolved in no time.",		/* [27] */		"Death, it seems, comes to us all...",/* Fairy */		/* [28] */		"You are almost hit before you realize you're "		"laughing...",		/* [29] */		"It's %mweapon isn't quite so funny anymore... ",		/* [30] */		"Wings ripped off, the fairy can't stand much more "		"of this.",		/* [31] */		"Bruised, you pant, waiting for the %mname to make "		"the next move.",		/* [32] */		"You sigh, thinking that fairies must all be born "		"idiots, as you attack.",		/* [33] */		"Your limbs afire, you raise your %uweapon in a "		"feeble defense.",		/* [34] */		"In only a small amount of pain, you think that "		"this fairy will soon be dead.",		/* [35] */		"This fight will be cake from now on...",		/* [36] */		"Death, it seems, comes to us all...",/* Insectoid */		/* [37] */		"Quaking, you remind yourself that this is only a "		"game... [grin]",		/* [38] */		"You shudder, knowing that this could very well be "		"the last thing you see.",		/* [39] */		"Surprised that it was this easy, you start to "		"finish the job...",		/* [40] */		"Bruised, you pant, waiting for the %mname to make "		"the next move.",		/* [41] */		"You sigh as you attack, wondering how far this will "		"go.",		/* [42] */		"Nearly lifeless, you stagger.",		/* [43] */		"Battered and bruised, you wonder how things will "		"turn out.",		/* [44] */		"Trusting your %uweapon, you get ready to attack "		"again.",		/* [45] */		"You don't think you can survive much longer either.",/* Fantastic */		/* [46] */		"You raise your %uweapon in salute to the beast's "		"death.",		/* [47] */		"flinching away, you realize that your %uweapon "		"won't help much now.",		/* [48] */		"Shrugging to yourself, you wonder at fate's little "		"quirks.",		/* [49] */		"Muscles sore, you decide to take things a bit more "		"carefully.",		/* [50] */		"Stepping closer, you feel as though you could take "		"on the world.",		/* [51] */		"The ambient magic in the air saps you, almost to "		"exhaustion.",		/* [52] */		"Now you're starting to question your skills in "		"combat.",		/* [53] */		"Trusting in lady luck, you prepare for the next "		"attack.",		/* [54] */		"You wonder if you'll survive even if you manage to "		"kill it. ",/* Elven */		/* [55] */		"You spit at the disgusting elf, wondering how they "		"survive so long.",		/* [56] */		"You feel as though anyone could kill you right now.",		/* [57] */		"Shrugging, you decide to carry out a death sentence.",		/* [58] */		"Hopefully you can take an equal amount as well.",		/* [59] */		"Barely scratched, you wonder who will be gone "		"before long.",		/* [60] */		"Almost lifeless, you sink to the ground in despair.",		/* [61] */		"You wonder how the insolent elf ever got so good...",		/* [62] */		"Clearly with the upper hand, you close with the "		"elf.",		/* [63] */		"In your mind you hear the church bells ringing your "		"funeral march.",/* FElemental */		/* [64] */		"You hope your armor really IS fireproof.",		/* [65] */		"Nearly spent, you clutch your %uweapon close.",		/* [66] */		"You pull out your waterbottle, threatening the "		"elemental.",		/* [67] */		"You don't feel so hot yourself.",		/* [68] */		"Fire was never a match for you.  It will be "		"extinguished.",		/* [69] */		"Shriveling, you feel the heat of a furnace on your "		"face.",		/* [70] */		"You begin to question the validity of this fight.",		/* [71] */		"Somehow, you believe you'll pull this one off.",		/* [72] */		"You begin to see spots in your vision.",/* WElemental */		/* [73] */		"Time to find out if you can swim.",		/* [74] */		"You are almost defeated.  You wonder at the "		"elemental's strength.",		/* [75] */		"You pull out a torch, waving it towards the pitiful "		"mass of water.",		/* [76] */		"Soaked in water, you circle your opponent warily.",		/* [77] */		"Whoever summoned this elemental should be shot.  "		"It was easy.",		/* [78] */		"You wonder who could be powerful enough to summon "		"such a creature.",		/* [79] */		"You wonder about your long dead grandmother.\n(And "		"what she has to do with any of this)",		/* [80] */		"You'll kill yourself if you don't survive this "		"fight. ",		/* [81] */		"Someone wants you dead.  It might happen soon.",/* EElemental */		/* [82] */		"You don't intend to give up your life very easily, "		"either.",		/* [83] */		"Nearly crushed by the powerful %mname you feel "		"dizzy.",		/* [84] */		"You fumble through your posessions, wondering if "		"any would have any effect on your opponent, the "		"%mname.",		/* [85] */		"Battered, you feel as though you have been buried "		"alive.",		/* [86] */		"You feel as though you could dispel this elemental "		"without any weapons.",		/* [87] */		"You feel amazed as the monster comes at you again.  "		"The sheer power of the thing stuns you.",		/* [88] */		"Sapped of only some strength, you are not yet "		"defeated.",		/* [89] */		"You stumble, but you know you are in far better "		"shape than your opponent.",		/* [90] */		"You vow that if you survive this, you'll kill "		"whoever sent this creature.",/* AElemental */		/* [91] */		"You wonder idly how long you can stand up to "		"elemental forces.",		/* [92] */		"Nearly to dead, you crawl out of reach of the "		"elemental.",		/* [93] */		"You hope to have this fight done quickly.  Lunch is "		"coming up.",		/* [94] */		"You wonder how badly it is wounded.",		/* [95] */		"You wonder if the %mname's dying will sound that "		"way.",		/* [96] */		"Truly outmatched, you want death to be quick.",		/* [97] */		"Almost suffocating, you wonder how the elemental "		"does it.",		/* [98] */		"You realize that the monster cannot stand against "		"you much longer.",		/* [99] */		"Death comes to us all.  Are you ready?",/* Dwarven */		/* [100] */		"You smile.  This will be fun.",		/* [101] */		"You cringe, hoping against hope that you will "		"survive.",		/* [102] */		"Glory in your eyes, you close in for the %mname's "		"destruction.",		/* [103] */		"You wonder how evenly matched you both are.",		/* [104] */		"You wonder if the %mname's dying will hurt very "		"badly.",		/* [105] */		"Fate against you, you prepare for the worst.",		/* [106] */		"Wounded, you watch the %mname carefully.",		/* [107] */		"You shudder at your wounds, at the pain.",		/* [108] */		"",/* Evil */		/* [109] */		"",		/* [110] */		"",		/* [111] */		"",		/* [112] */		"",		/* [113] */		"",		/* [114] */		"",		/* [115] */		"",		/* [116] */		"",		/* [117] */		"",/* Good */		/* [118] */		"",		/* [119] */		"",		/* [120] */		"",		/* [121] */		"",		/* [122] */		"",		/* [123] */		"",		/* [124] */		"",		/* [125] */		"",		/* [126] */		"",/* Flying */		/* [127] */		"",		/* [128] */		"",		/* [129] */		"",		/* [130] */		"",		/* [131] */		"",		/* [132] */		"",		/* [133] */		"",		/* [134] */		"",		/* [135] */		"",/* Undead */		/* [136] */		"",		/* [137] */		"",		/* [138] */		"",		/* [139] */		"",		/* [140] */		"",		/* [141] */		"",		/* [142] */		"",		/* [143] */		"",		/* [144] */		"",/* Psychic */		/* [145] */		"You've heard stories that such an enemy can mount an "		"invisible attack, so you ready your %uweapon.",		/* [146] */		"You struggle to regain your strength, but can't "		"seem to find it.",		/* [147] */		"Deciding the %mname is no match for a hero as "		"yourself, you close for the kill.",		/* [148] */		"You realize you've began to send harm the %mname's "		"way, but then you have your own wounds as well.",		/* [149] */		"You realize the %mname is weakening and ready your "		"uweapon for a charge.",		/* [150] */		"You hope the end will come soon, as your weakened "		"muscles don't seem to respond.",		/* [151] */		"Being a hero, you don't let the %mname's calmness "		"affect you, although your wounds begin to burn with "		"pain.",		/* [152] */		"Though you've seen better days, you see the dispair "		"in the %mname's eyes and close for the kill.",		/* [153] */		"You hope the %mname will drop its weapon, but "		"wonder if you could find the strength to finish it "		"if it did.",/* Other */		/* [154] */		"You wonder where such a creature could come from as "		"you ready your %uweapon for attack.",		/* [155] */		"You decide to attack the %mname, but your muscles "		"don't seem to respond.",		/* [156] */		"Being the hero you are, you feel no mercy.",		/* [157] */		"You don't quite feel the zip of adrenaline you felt "		"at the beginning of the battle yourself.",		/* [158] */		"As for yourself, you feel as well as ever.",		/* [159] */		"You wonder if you can go on at all... what a hero.",		/* [160] */		"You don't quite feel your usual self, but still have "		"plenty of strength left and continue battle.",		/* [161] */		"You begin to catch your second wind as you ready "		"your %uweapon to finish of the %mname.",		/* [162] */		"Your hopes mirror those of the %mname, but death "		"must come to us all."	}};resource 'STR#' (128, "Monster Text Combat Strings") {	{	/* array StringArray: 181 elements *//* Humanoid */		/* [1] */		"The healthy %mname sputters words in an almost "		"familiar language.",		/* [2] */		"The insidious %mname circles you warily waiting for "		"an opening.",		/* [3] */		"The nearly fallen %mname struggles to keep out of "		"your weapon's reach.",		/* [4] */		"The slightly wounded %mname eyes your %uweapon "		"warily.",				/* [5] */		"The pitiful %mname raises it's %mweapon not yet "		"ready to give up the fight.",		/* [6] */		"The %mname looks slightly weary, but it looks FAR "		"better than you feel.",		/* [7] */		"The %mname looks at you, hate in it's eyes.",		/* [8] */		"The %mname nearly falls over it's %mweapon as it "		"backs away from you.",		/* [9] */		"Badly wounded, the %mname backs out of reach, "		"trying to keep away.",/* Orc */		/* [10] */		"The %mname sputters words in a challenging orcish "		"tongue.",		/* [11] */		"The insidious %mname circles you, eyes darting "		"towards your coin purse.",		/* [12] */		"Nearly defeated, the %mname struggles to take any "		"opportunity possible.",		/* [13] */		"Only slightly shaken, the %mname licks a gash on "		"it's forearm,\nsnarls an orcish curse, and spits "		"blood at you.",		/* [14] */		"The shaken %mname readies itself,  not yet ready to "		"forsake winning.",		/* [15] */		"The %mname limps slightly, but quickly steps "		"toward you.",		/* [16] */		"%mname Raises it's %mweapon above it's head, and "		"charges.",		/* [17] */		"The %mname backs away, eyes pleading for mercy.",		/* [18] */		"The %mname nearly trips as it backs off.",/* Goblin */		/* [19] */		"The small %mname screeches at you in Goblin.",		/* [20] */		"The sniveling %mname jumps up and down, rushing you "		"for all it's worth.",		/* [21] */		"Almost gone, the %mname wearily stands, waiting for "		"your move.",		/* [22] */		"%mname stands slightly downhill, but you have taken "		"more wounds.",		/* [23] */		"The shaken %mname took a few hits, but this isn't "		"over.",		/* [24] */		"The %mweapon gleams, and you suddenly know what "		"death really means.",		/* [25] */		"A smile flashes across the %mname's face as it "		"closes.",		/* [26] */		"The %mname is in a near frenzy, death closing in.",		/* [27] */		"%mweapon and %uweapon clash together, both "		"combatants panting . ",/* Fairy */		/* [28] */		"The small %mname charges, tiny %mweapon raised in "		"defiance.",		/* [29] */		"The flying %mname hoovers near, tiny weapon raised.",		/* [30] */		"The %mname looks at you almost accusingly, as it "		"curses your mother's child.",		/* [31] */		"A determined fairy looks back, undaunted by it's "		"small wounds.",		/* [32] */		"The %mname looks up at you, ready to finish what is "		"necessary.",		/* [33] */		"%mname looks at you, hate budding in it's eyes.  "		"This won't be pretty.",		/* [34] */		"A triumphant gurgle comes from the small fairy as "		"it closes.",		/* [35] */		"The %mname thrashes in pain, knowing death is near.",		/* [36] */		"Both you and the %mname try to look fine, but it "		"just doesn't work.",/* Insectoid */		/* [37] */		"Chittering, the strange %mname looks at you through "		"many eyes.",		/* [38] */		"The inhuman appendages of the %mname hoover over "		"you, ready to kill.",		/* [39] */		"Nearly dead, the %mname struggles to remain "		"coherent.",		/* [40] */		"The %mname's eyes glitter with hatred.",		/* [41] */		"The %mname looks worn, but will not be done so "		"easily.",		/* [42] */		"The insectoid slashes above you, %mweapon whizzing "		"through the air.'",		/* [43] */		"Undaunted, the %mname's pincers wiggle in "		"anticipation of a meal.",		/* [44] */		"The insect thrashes in pain, knowing death is "		"near.",		/* [45] */		"Blood is rushing from the %mname's body.",/* Fantastic */		/* [46] */		"The %mname has an aura of power radiating from it.",		/* [47] */		"The inhuman %mname looks for an opening to finish "		"you off.",		/* [48] */		"Drained, the %mname almost withers when you look at "		"it.",		/* [49] */		"The magical crea